# Passkeys backend TODO

Generated by the light-it auth package. `auth:setup` wrote the passkey
registration API: a signed-in user adds, lists, renames and deletes their
passkeys. Passkey login is not part of this layer yet. No boilerplate file
needs editing. Delete this file once you've read it.

## What to do

1. Run `php artisan migrate` to create the `passkeys` table.
2. Set the relying party in `.env` (read by `config/passkeys.php`):

   ```dotenv
   PASSKEYS_RP_ID=localhost
   PASSKEYS_RP_NAME="${APP_NAME}"
   PASSKEYS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
   ```

   `PASSKEYS_RP_ID` is the frontend's host (or a registrable parent domain),
   without scheme or port. `PASSKEYS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` lists the full frontend
   origins, comma-separated.
3. Optionally set `PASSKEYS_USER_HANDLE_SECRET`; it falls back to `APP_KEY`.
   It keys the user handle stored on every authenticator, so changing it (or
   rotating `APP_KEY` while it is the fallback) breaks every passkey
   registered before the change.
4. Use a cache store shared by every app server (the boilerplate's `database`
   store works): the registration challenge lives there.

## Endpoints

All under `auth:sanctum` in `routes/passkeys.php`, which `routes/api.php`
requires. Every route but the list uses `throttle:passkeys` (6 a minute per
user, 30 per IP), registered by `lightit-auth-laravel`'s own service provider
when `\Lightit\Authentication\Domain\PasskeyRateLimiter` exists, so the
package must stay a runtime dependency.

| Method | Path | Body | Answer |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/passkeys` | - | `200`: `id`, `name`, `created_at`, `last_used_at` per passkey |
| `POST` | `/passkeys/registration-options` | `{ password }` | `200`: WebAuthn creation options |
| `POST` | `/passkeys` | `{ name, credential }` | `201`: the new passkey; `410` expired or replayed challenge, `422` failed verification, `409` already registered |
| `PATCH` | `/passkeys/{passkey}` | `{ name }` | `200`: the renamed passkey |
| `POST` | `/passkeys/{passkey}/delete` | `{ password }` | `204` |

Starting a registration and deleting a passkey ask for the current password,
like turning 2FA on and off; a wrong one is a `422` on `password`, not a
`401`. Another user's passkey is a `403`. `credential` is the browser's
`RegistrationResponseJSON`, sent as is. The challenge is bound to the user,
lives `passkeys.challenge_ttl_seconds` and is spent by the first
`POST /passkeys` under a cache lock. Every call into `web-auth/webauthn-lib`
lives in `\Lightit\Authentication\Domain\Services\PasskeyCeremonyService`.
